turnip-rt-v3.patch is the original 33-commit series, exported with:
    git format-patch --stdout <base>..<tip>
SHA256: 2b597d666d31d63d0659dbd6508ec98ee24f7b03b32e6e3c47fe56edab12f445
It is included for review and recovery, not applied a second time by the build.
The dedicated builder fetches the pinned tip, not the moving branch.

kgsl-aqe-enable.patch fixes an omission in that series: tu_kgsl_get_aqe()
was added, but its result was not assigned to device->has_aqe in the KGSL
physical-device loader. Without this assignment VK_KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline
stays hidden. The patch queries KGSL_PROP_IS_AQE_ENABLED (0x30); it does not
force or bypass the kernel's answer. RT also requires the existing SW-fuse
check and the device's nonzero max_rt_threads property.

The native RT variant uses the repository's common KGSL synchronization
fixes and A840v2 chip-ID correction. Ordinary Mesa-main variants are unchanged.
The experimental A8xx mesh/wave32 patch series is not included in this variant.

